<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tribute extraction</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tribute extraction is the recurring pattern by which empires drew wealth from conquered or subordinate peoples through regular payments in goods, precious metals, labour or captives, rather than through direct administration. It allowed rapid expansion at low administrative cost, but bred resentment among subjects and often collapsed when military pressure weakened. The Assyrian and Aztec empires depended heavily on tribute, as did steppe powers such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>.</p></div>
